# APT suites published to GitHub Pages by scripts/build-apt-repo.sh.
#
# One line per supported distro codename, whitespace separated:
#   <suite>  <family>  <description...>
#
# <suite>  is the APT suite/codename served under dists/<suite>/ and must equal
#          the distro codename used in the package version suffix (`~<suite>`),
#          which is how source-built .debs are routed to their suite.
# <family> is `ubuntu` or `debian`. Binaries that are pinned per distro family
#          rather than built per suite (the passt .debs, whose release asset
#          names carry `_ubuntu_` / `_debian_`) are published to every suite of
#          that family.
noble     ubuntu  Ubuntu 24.04 (noble)
resolute  ubuntu  Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute)
trixie    debian  Debian 13 (trixie)
